\section*{Notation}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
$h(x,t)$ & flow depth (m) \\
$q(x,t)$ & unit discharge (m$^2$/s) \\
$z_b(x,t)$ & bed elevation (m) \\
$C_f$ & friction coefficient \\
$\Delta t, \Delta x$ & time step and grid spacing \\
$\epsilon$ & regularisation parameter of the friction law \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\medskip
\noindent Throughout the paper the small parameter of the regularised
friction law is denoted $\varepsilon$; its role is defined in
Section~2.
